{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_016rN6zFcsSwW3BnKwr6z16K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All verification is complete. The blocker F-EPIC-001 is independently disproven against the current code (SDK guard, CLI repro fails closed, tests at all three layers), NB-2 and NB-5 are verified fixed, F-EPIC-002 is fixed except the minor unknown-field leg (runtime-confirmed still tolerated), NB-1/NB-4 remain open by design, and both gates pass (green-verify: 118 tests + immutability OK; verify-all: 132 tests, lint, boundaries, exit 0).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"outcome\": \"ready-for-closeout\",\n  \"confirmedIssues\": [\n    \"F-EPIC-002 (residual leg, minor, non-blocking): unknown extra fields on read-back thread references are still silently tolerated — only intake-stream messageEvents/listEvents run the closed ThreadRef schema (validateThreadRef, pipeline.ts:92, 267); listMessages, listTurns, and both listQueuedWork route through resolveThreadRef, which now rejects blank paths but does not name unknown ref fields. Runtime-confirmed this pass: messages.listMessages({ filePath: <valid>, bogusField: 42 }) returns ok. The material legs of F-EPIC-002 are fixed and test-covered: empty path now returns caller_error/invalid_thread_ref on all five read surfaces (epic-fix.test.ts), and all four CLI read commands have the missing-flag usage guard (verified live: `messages list` → missing_flag). Behavior remains fail-closed; this matches the fix batch's stated scope.\",\n    \"NB-1 (minor, human ruling pending, non-blocking): empty-string payload text and tool_result.content still pass validation (validate.ts unmodified, Schema.String at lines 55/63) while other required fields use NonEmptyString. Deliberately out of scope for the fix batch per artifacts/fix/001-epic-fix-batch.md; the epic-prose vs tech-design conflict still needs a ruling and an erratum on whichever document loses.\",\n    \"NB-4 (observation, accepted): setIntakeWalkHook/setIntakeClock module seams remain in pipeline.ts, unchanged by design — sanctioned by the test plan's architecture-risk rows, inert when unset, confined by the boundary check.\",\n    \"Carried unresolved item: Epic 02 must own adding the work_item status-vocabulary constraint so 'queued'-only is not silently relied on (unchanged from canonical review).\",\n    \"New, trivial (fix-touched surface): team-impl-log.md's Epic Closeout section retains stale duplicate lines ('Epic Fix Status: not-started', 'Epic Reverify Status: not-started') below the updated entries — tracking-log hygiene only.\"\n  ],\n  \"disputedOrUnconfirmedIssues\": [],\n  \"readinessAssessment\": \"The sole blocker F-EPIC-001 is disproven by the current code and independently re-verified this pass: threads.newThread rejects empty/whitespace-only paths with caller_error/invalid_thread_ref before any storage touch (src/domains/threads/index.ts:91), resolveThreadRef mirrors the guard for every read surface (threads/index.ts:177), and the original repro on the freshly built CLI (`threads new-thread --file-path '' --registry <clean>`) now exits 1 with the structured error and creates no registry file. Coverage exists at all three layers: SDK (empty, whitespace-only, resolveThreadRef legs), in-process CLI, and spawned dist/cli.js (cli-process-fix.test.ts, registered in vitest.config.ts under LHC_PROCESS_SUITE). NB-2 is fixed (parseArgs strict:true; unknown_flag structured error naming the offending flag, e.g. --titel/--file-pth, tested at both boundaries) and NB-5 is fixed (notImplemented() gone from src/, prebuild clean added, stale dist/commands|thread-events|token-counting absent after rebuild). Both gates pass on the current tree: green-verify (12 files / 118 tests, Red-manifest immutability OK over 15 files) and verify-all (build, typecheck, lint OK 44 files, boundaries OK 40 files, 18 files / 132 tests, exit 0). The fix-batch CLI envelope failures recorded in artifacts/fix/00